**A third operand shape, and the third scale.** `CThreatTrigger` derives from `CTagTrigger`, so slot 7 takes the *country*, and its own `LoadKey` (0x5F2CC0, recorded, keys `which` and `value`) parses `value` with plain `atoi` into **+0x48** - not through `TokenToFixedPoint`. Evaluate then multiplies by 1000. So `threat = 50` is fifty points of threat and `threat = 50.5` is read as 50: the decimals a `CValueTrigger` keyword accepts are silently unavailable here. `CRelationTrigger::LoadKey` (0x5DDE50, recorded) does the same thing into the same +0x48, and its Evaluate multiplies by 1000 the same way. `CAllOrganisationPopularityTrigger::LoadKey` (0x5FA760) also uses `atoi`, but multiplies by 1000 at load and keeps two values, `organisation` at +0x44 and `popularity` at +0x48.

**`controlled_by`, four argument forms, and it is false on a scope with no province.** 0x5DFAB0 to 0x5DFC2C; 14 int3 before, 4 after; **five** `ret 4` (0x5DFB9C, 0x5DFBC9, 0x5DFBF2, 0x5DFC13, 0x5DFC29) all restoring the same SEH slot `[esp+0x1C]`, so it is one function (trap 3, benign).

    if (scope->province (+0x28) == 0) return false
    p = g_CCurrentGameState (0x1A89790) ->+0xB8C [scope->province]
    if (this->arg_is_this (+0x18))  return p->controller_id (+0x338) == EventScope_GetCountryTag(scope).id
    if (this->arg_is_from (+0x19))  return p->controller_id == scope->from_country_id (+0x1C)
    if (this->is_owner (+0x48))     return p->controller_id == p->owner_id (+0x330)
    else                            return p->controller_id == this->tag id (+0x44)

The third arm is **`controlled_by = owner`**: CControlledByTrigger::LoadArgument (0x5DF9D0) sets the byte at +0x48 on token 0x1EC, so the form asks "is this province not occupied". `owned_by` has no such arm (COwnedByTrigger::Evaluate, 0x5DF250).

`controlled_by` on a country-only scope is **false, not an error** - the same shape as an unresolvable context.
